=== accessibility-focus-notes.md ===
# v36 conversation focus/accessibility harness notes

Work is limited to `scripts/conversation-ui/check-focus.cjs` in the root-verified v36 checkout (main prefix `1071a525`, tree prefix `47c535`). Read AGENTS.md, the current continuation marker, P2 preview constraints, existing focus harness, real ConversationPreview/StagingConsole and their existing local doubles before editing. No application component, shared style, source policy, SQL, setting, dependency or runtime route was changed by this agent.

## Current outcome: prepared and unrun in Chromium

The original 20 focus/layout checks are preserved. Nineteen additional mode probes are prepared, for a planned 39 checks if a future complete browser run passes. **Zero new browser probes were executed; no screenshots or reproduced application defects are claimed.** Root reported that no runnable Chromium was available and its single normal runtime preparation could not obtain a valid browser archive. This agent did not repeat installation or environment probes or substitute another browser surface lacking the required viewport/media controls. All 37 native PostgreSQL cases remain independently prepared/unrun.

Initial static preparation evidence is `/workspace/scratch/500c5aa1eb33/v36/focus-initial/preparation-status.json`, explicitly marked PREPARED_UNRUN with browserExecuted:false, browserChecksPassed:0 and an empty screenshot list. It preserves the initial pre-format script and bundle hashes. `focus-initial/production.css` preserves the actual generated production CSS used for bundling. This is static evidence, not computed browser styling or visual acceptance.

## Prepared added coverage

The existing real React/Radix fixtures still use fictional local service/Auth-operation doubles, with no application route. New probes use three independent modes at 390×844:

- Controlled 200% font enlargement: computed root and body baselines are both doubled inside the fixture (expected baseline root16px/body18px to root32px/body36px). The test records actual before/after root, body, heading, button, representative paragraph and composer sizes. It requires representative control text to double and visualViewport.scale to remain1. This method is explicitly not native browser text zoom or WCAG conformance.
- Reduced-motion emulation: actual media-query state, dialog computed animation/transition durations and runtime animation records are captured; the current global short-duration rule is asserted.
- Forced-colour emulation: actual media-query state, keyboard focus-visible state, outline width/style/colour, background/border/shadow and forced-colour adjustment are recorded. Focus must remain visibly outlined rather than relying on a suppressed shadow ring. The staging Christian-content switch must retain a distinguishable thumb/track without changing its setting.

Each mode covers staging Delete/Cancel, navigation Cancel, Stop during a pending local append, preview Finish/Keep working, preview switch Cancel and preview Retry/Stop. Checks require sequential Tab reachability, unobscured controls after keyboard scrolling, unclipped control text, narrow page/dialog bounds and Tab/Shift+Tab dialog containment. Escape or deliberate Cancel/Keep restores the exact opener and fictional draft. Preview retry retains a newer unsent draft. Stop remains reachable during pending work.

Only the preview Retry/Stop interval pauses the fixture clock so a canned response cannot finish before keyboard traversal. The installed Playwright type declarations confirm the existing install/pauseAt/resume APIs. The clock is installed once, paused at its current time plus1second and resumed in finally. This is explicitly labelled a controlled fictional pending interval, not evidence about application/provider timing. No production deadline or implementation changes.

New HTTP fetch, WebSocket, peer-connection and microphone/display-capture guards record forbidden attempts; the existing all-request routing still aborts any unexpected document/resource transport. Results must show no forbidden attempts or blocked unexpected requests. No real SDK/Auth/provider/device is invoked by the fixtures. Source rendering remains exactly the existing real components and source strings; no SRT wording or policy is changed.

Generated production CSS is now required for these style/layout assertions, rather than silently skipping them. The harness records its absolute path and SHA-256 and copies it into the evidence directory. Each future probe records media/fonts/style/bounds observations and saves a screenshot or a failure screenshot; failed probes remain failed in the aggregate. This browser-only evidence does not yet exist for the new modes.

## Static validation and diagnostics

- `node --check scripts/conversation-ui/check-focus.cjs`: passed.
- Both actual esbuild fixture bundles compiled with the generated production CSS while an in-memory wrapper removed the final main invocation. No browser launch or page execution occurred.
- Initial compiled preview fixture: 1,963,578 bytes, SHA-256 `7c0d5663a27062a70f5bc2a4f427cf3ba497cf4e2060dc9583082065b9ac0047`.
- Initial compiled staging fixture: 1,475,008 bytes, SHA-256 `d5c039d5d633c6fc6ae07527713a9d8bbd823c58b5ab258b429d47310c203f98`.
- Production CSS: `/workspace/scratch/500c5aa1eb33/v36/repo/.output/public/assets/styles-DuOMzkts.css`, SHA-256 `83f967bcb9eb8de6df69b5f08b191eb607fb0d33c7517b40c6ef94e3e1ef44f9`.
- Initial scoped ESLint reported four formatting-only findings around the animation mapping expression after standalone formatting. Repository ESLint --fix corrected those; `focus-lint-initial.log`, `focus-lint-correction.log` and `focus-lint-final.log` preserve the sequence. Final scoped ESLint passes.
- Independent review requested one narrow strengthening: forced-colour outline colour must differ from the control background. This was added before freeze, without weakening other checks.

Final frozen harness SHA-256: `96ae59ca9162db2e35d6981aa060e1001ae5e88bda00cb35ab8ae5d6f1c77c00`. Root/reviewer own final independent bundle-only verification and the wider checkpoint evidence. Previous browser keyboard results remain historical, not rerun results for this changed harness.

## Future reproduction once a browser runtime is available

Use the existing harness and explicit installed paths; do not substitute viewport/pinch scaling for font enlargement or label static bundles as browser acceptance:

```
BFA_PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/opt/codex/runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/node_modules/playwright BFA_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=/absolute/installed/chromium BFA_UI_CSS=/absolute/current/generated-production.css node scripts/conversation-ui/check-focus.cjs /absolute/new-focus-evidence
```

Inspect the preserved failure observations/screenshots first, then fix only reproduced component/style defects. Potential issues suggested by source—nowrap/fixed-height controls, centered tall dialogs and shadow-only forced-colour focus—remain hypotheses, not confirmed defects. No speculative application fix was made.

