## Prepared coverage

All original VoiceControls checks are preserved. The new layout/media cases now require a nonempty `BFA_UI_CSS` rather than silently reporting layout success without production styles. The report records the exact CSS path/hash and checks actual computed flex layout before interpreting geometry.

Five prepared modes reuse the same real VoiceControls, ConversationService and ConversationVoiceBinding with deferred fictional resource/provider ports:

1. 320 CSS-pixel viewport, controlled root font doubled, body unchanged.
2. 320 CSS-pixel viewport, controlled root font and separately computed body font both doubled.
3. 390 CSS-pixel viewport with reduced-motion preference.
4. 390 CSS-pixel viewport with forced colours.
5. 320 CSS-pixel viewport combining controlled root/body doubling, reduced motion and forced colours.

The technique is explicit inline fixture sizing derived from observed baseline computed fonts. The intended usual root change is 16 to 32 px and the current source's fixed body size is 18 px, separately doubled to 36 px in the body-enlargement modes. These numeric browser observations are still unrun. At execution, the harness records actual root, body, inherited fixture copy, button and status font sizes before/after, requires the intended ratios and requires visualViewport.scale to stay 1. It does not call viewport/pinch scaling genuine text zoom, and it does not claim that root-only sizing enlarges all text.

Each prepared mode follows seven actual current states: idle, active, changing input, paused, closing, shutdown failed and retrying. It uses the unchanged real long labels/status wording, including Finish talking and Retry shutdown. It records document/element geometry, text rectangles, scroll extents and screenshots; asserts no clipping or horizontal overflow; and preserves the existing 44px control minimum.

Actual keyboard navigation and activation exercise Start, Mute, Unmute, Stop answer, Pause, Resume, Finish talking, Type instead and Retry shutdown. The real service still cancels its fictional turn and rejects the deliberately late reply. Mode evidence includes keyboard focus-visible state, target rectangle, outline style/width/colour, background and shadow. Forced-colour focus requires a visible computed outline rather than relying only on a box-shadow ring. Status focus fallback is also inspected. No assertion is weakened because a browser is unavailable.

Reduced-motion and forced-colour media must match their requested runtime values. Reduced-motion checks inspect actual computed transition/animation durations and any running document animations. This is prepared browser evidence, not currently observed behaviour or a screen-reader/WCAG conformance claim.

Existing transport/WebSocket interception and real microphone rejection remain in place. The fixture resources are fictional, and application routes remain inactive. Runtime errors, blocked requests and attempted real microphone access still fail the harness.

