# Independent conversation accessibility review

6 November 2026. Scope: the existing transport-blocked conversation preview, fictional staging console and inactive VoiceControls fixtures. No authored content, clinical policy, private-writing rule, runtime activation or service/SQL behavior is in scope.

## Initial source and harness review

Read repository `AGENTS.md`, the latest continuation completion/next-task block, `p2-preview-checkpoint.md`, both existing browser harnesses, the actual conversation components, shared dialog/button primitives and relevant production CSS.

The earlier checkpoint explicitly leaves enlarged text, reduced motion and forced colours unverified for these conversation surfaces. Its ordinary keyboard/mobile checks and the separate completed ten-day journey root-font checks remain historical evidence, not new results of this batch.

Review requirements sent to the two harness authors:

- Label the enlargement technique precisely: a controlled root font of 32px compared with 16px, at the same CSS viewport and scale. Record actual representative computed text sizes. This is not browser/native text zoom, pinch zoom or proof that every text node doubled. Production body text is fixed at 18px (19px at wide viewports), so root-font enlargement alone does not enlarge inherited pixel-sized body copy.
- Verify reduced-motion media activation and actual computed animation/transition durations and runtime animation state. Existing production CSS already reduces animation and transition durations to 0.001ms; asserting only a media preference is insufficient.
- Verify forced-colour activation together with computed and visible keyboard focus/boundaries. A nominal focus state or shadow-only focus ring is insufficient. Inspect actual screenshots as well as measurements.
- Keep actual dialogs keyboard-reachable, including Tab/Shift+Tab containment, Escape/Cancel focus restoration and exact unsent draft preservation. Enlarged long labels and taller dialogs must remain reachable without horizontal clipping.
- Retain blocked HTTP/WebSocket behavior and explicit microphone guards. Count real API attempts separately from intentionally fictional service/resource calls. No live Auth, microphone, provider or persistence acceptance may be inferred.

Potential source targets are not yet confirmed defects: Button defaults to fixed height and nowrap; Dialog and AlertDialog center fixed content without explicit maximum height or scrolling. Any repair must follow actual reproduced evidence.

The component import audit shows the shared Button/Dialog/AlertDialog are consumed by the conversation components; their remaining references are unused UI helper components. Journey routes use their own controls and classes. Shared global styling changes would warrant targeted journey regression; a source-verified conversation-only repair does not justify replaying the completed journey audit.

## Execution status

The installed Playwright package did not have a usable Chromium runtime. The root task preserved one normal setup failure and a diagnostic showing the official archive endpoint returned a 195-byte HTML “Site Unavailable” response, not a browser archive. The inspected fallback lacked the necessary media, viewport and fixture-routing capabilities. This reviewer did not install anything, repeat setup, launch a browser or substitute mock layout observations.

All new browser modes/probes remain prepared and **unrun**, as do the existing baseline browser workflows in this batch. There are no screenshots or newly observed UI defects. No application fix, layout pass, forced-colour result, reduced-motion result or visual accessibility acceptance is claimed.

## Final prepared source review

The focus harness preserves its twenty original checks and adds nineteen probes across three requested modes at 390×844: controlled root/body enlargement, reduced motion and forced colours. It records baseline/current computed font sizes and scale, actual media values, page/dialog bounds, focus styling and runtime animation data. Tab and Shift+Tab containment, Cancel/Keep/Escape restoration, exact drafts, pending staging Stop and preview Retry/Stop remain assertions on real components with fictional operation doubles. A paused Playwright clock holds only the fictional retry-response interval; the code resumes it in `finally` and does not call this production timing acceptance. The forced-colour switch probe checks actual thumb/track distinction without a shadow. Review added the explicit focused-outline/background inequality before freeze.

The VoiceControls harness preserves the original service/binding lifecycle checks and prepares five modes: root-only enlargement and separate root+body enlargement at 320px, reduced motion and forced colours at 390px, and the combined enlarged/reduced/forced mode at 320px. Seven current states, nine actual action labels, keyboard/focus state, document/control geometry, unclipped text, original 44px minimum controls, actual computed durations and runtime animations are covered by prepared assertions. No fictional resource callback is represented as a real microphone/provider call.

The fixed production body font means the distinction between root-only and root+body enlargement matters. Both scripts explicitly describe controlled fixture sizing and record actual ratios; neither presents viewport/pinch scaling as native text zoom. Actual browser values still await execution.

Both harnesses now reject absent or empty production CSS instead of silently skipping styled checks. Their evidence binds the exact supplied CSS hash; a hash alone does not establish freshness against arbitrary caller source. For this checkpoint, the stylesheet is the output of the successful baseline build while all 455 application source files remained byte-identical to the preceding checkpoint, with no added source files. Future browser execution must rebuild immediately before freezing and recording its source/CSS evidence. Fixtures omit the app root's external Google-font stylesheet and therefore use locally available fallback fonts; they do not establish hosted typography or full-route rendering.

No blocking source-review finding remains for saving this prepared harness extension. This is not acceptance of the unexecuted browser assertions.

## Independent non-browser verification

- Two frozen harness files passed `node --check`.
- Invoked the actual existing esbuild `bundle()` functions for preview, staging and VoiceControls. An in-memory copy removed only the final automatic `main().catch(...)` invocation and exported the existing functions. The repository scripts were not modified for this check. Browser launch was trapped; the launch counter remained zero.
- All three generated HTML fixtures contained the exact production CSS and their compiled JavaScript parsed successfully. HTML sizes were 1,963,578 bytes (preview), 1,475,008 bytes (staging) and 1,607,411 bytes (VoiceControls).
- Four independent guard checks passed: missing and empty CSS each rejected before browser launch in each harness. These are configuration checks, not browser-mode tests.
- Both harness hashes remained unchanged during the independent checks. No browser checks, media emulation, keyboard interaction, geometry inspection or screenshot capture ran.

Evidence: `independent-harness-syntax.log`, `independent-combined-bundle.log`, `independent-static-summary.json`, `independent-bundle/result.json`, and the scratch-only reproducible `review-bundle-check.cjs`. The earlier independent VoiceControls-only bundle run remains in `independent-voice-bundle.log`. Authors retain their scoped lint and bundle diagnostics separately; the focus lint initially had four formatting findings that were corrected, not UI failures.

